# iOS constraints (PWA chrome)

This app is used on iPhone (Simulator Safari + home-screen PWA). `viewportFit` is `cover`, so the page draws under the Dynamic Island and the home indicator. **Every layout change must leave those insets alone.** Desktop `lg:` fills are not proof.

`env(safe-area-inset-*)` is ~47–59px top and ~34px bottom on iPhone. It is `0` on Android/desktop and in Chrome device mode. Never judge insets from Chrome.

## The four edges

| Edge | What sits there | How |
|---|---|---|
| Top | status bar / Dynamic Island | `.app-top-bar` / `PageHeader` only. Padding, not `top: env(...)`. |
| Bottom | home indicator + tab bar | `.app-bottom-bar` on the nav. Page body: shell `pb-[calc(4rem+env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]`. |
| Left / right | notch in landscape + gutter | `.px-app` / header padding. Not a second gutter on cards. |
| Keyboard | iOS visual viewport | Chat composer hook. Do not use `100vh` for anything the keyboard can cover. |

```tsx
// ✅
<PageHeader><h1 className="text-s font-semibold">Inbox</h1></PageHeader>
<nav className="app-bottom-bar fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0">…</nav>

// ❌ pad main for the clock (double gap)
<main className="pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]">

// ❌ one-off env on a Tailwind class (preflight wins; home indicator covers labels)
<nav className="pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]">

// ❌ desktop fill that also runs on the phone
<div className="h-dvh">          // use lg:h-dvh
<div className="h-[100vh-220px]"> // magic number; ignores nav + insets
```

## Phone vs desktop

Below `1024` / `lg:` the phone has a **bottom nav** and columns **stack**. Do not make phone columns fill the viewport. `lg:h-dvh` / `lg:h-full` is desktop only.

A viewport fill must subtract, on that breakpoint: header (`.app-top-bar`) + bottom nav (`4rem`) + `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` when the nav is showing.

## Type on iOS

iOS inflates `<button>` / field text to 16px. Shirt sizes live in unlayered `.text-xs` / `.text-s`. Put pill labels on an inner `span`, not only on the `<button>`. Keep the 16px floor on `input` / `textarea` / `select` (coarse pointers) so iOS does not zoom.

## Must

- Inset classes live in `globals.css` **outside `@layer`**: `.app-top-bar`, `.app-top-bar-tall`, `.app-bottom-bar`, `.px-app`
- One top inset per screen — do not stack `PageHeader` on another `app-top-bar`
- Do not change `viewportFit: "cover"` or `statusBarStyle: "black-translucent"` per page
- After header, board height, nav, or gutter work: refresh **iOS Simulator Safari** at `http://localhost:3000`. Desktop looking right is not enough.

## Do not

- `if (isIOS) return <IOSHeader />`
- `h-12` / `h-14` on a bar that also has `padding-top: env(...)`
- Treat Chrome device mode as iPhone
